=head1 ATTRIBUTES

Each name works in C<\%attributes>, and as a C<set_> method that returns the element.

=over

=item C<application_reconnect>

Whether the WebSocket connection to the application should be reconnected if it drops during the call. Defaults to false True or false.

=item C<asr_smart_format>

Whether smart formatting should be applied to transcripts. Takes precedence over deepgramSmartFormat True or false.

=item C<backgroundnoisereduction>

This parameters enables background noise filtering on the audio stream before it reaches the STT engine, improving transcription accuracy in noisy environments

=item C<customer_name>

Customer name sent to Conversations and Conversational Intelligence. Defaults to the caller ID

=item C<debug>

Multiple debug options to be used for troubleshooting

=item C<deepgramsmartformat>

This parameter enables Deepgram's smart formatting feature, which automatically applies punctuation, capitalization, and formatting (e.g. numbers, dates, currency) to transcripts

=item C<dtmf_detection>

Whether DTMF tones should be detected and reported in speech transcription True or false.

=item C<eager_eot_threshold>

Eager end-of-turn confidence threshold, which fires before the end-of-turn threshold. The value can be between 0.3 and 0.9

=item C<echo_prompt_filtering>

Whether transcripts that echo the agent's own text-to-speech should be dropped. Defaults to false True or false.

=item C<elevenlabs_language_text_normalization>

Legacy alias of ttsLanguageTextNormalization True or false.

=item C<elevenlabs_text_normalization>

When using ElevenLabs as TTS provider, this parameter allows you to enable or disable its text normalization feature

=item C<events>

This parameter allows you to enable event subscriptions

=item C<hints>

Phrases to help better accuracy in speech recognition of these pharases

=item C<ignorebackchannel>

This parameter brief caller acknowledgments (e.g. "yeah", "uh-huh") are ignored and will not interrupt the agent while it is speaking.

=item C<include_in_prompt>

Extra fields to be included in prompt messages. The value can be turn-state or prompt-segments

=item C<intelligence_service>

The Conversational Intelligence Service id or unique name to be used for the session

=item C<interrupt_sensitivity>

Set the sensitivity of the interrupt feature for speech. The value can be low, medium, or high

=item C<interruptible>

Whether and how the input from a caller, such as speaking or DTMF can interrupt the play of text-to-speech

=item C<language>

Language to be used for both text-to-speech and transcription

=item C<partial_prompt_on_hangup>

Whether the in-progress partial transcript should be reported as a prompt when the call hangs up True or false.

=item C<partial_prompts>

Whether partial prompts should be reported to WebSocket server before the caller finishes speaking True or false.

=item C<preemptible>

Whether subsequent text-to-speech or play media can interrupt the on-going play of text-to-speech or media True or false.

=item C<profanity_filter>

Whether profanities should be filtered out of the speech transcription True or false.

=item C<report_input_during_agent_speech>

Whether prompts should be reported to WebSocket server when text-to-speech playing and interrupt is disabled True or false.

=item C<speech_model>

Speech model to be used for transcription

=item C<speechtimeout>

Set the duration of silence that indicates the end of speech

=item C<transcription_language>

Language to be used for transcription

=item C<transcription_provider>

Provider to be used for transcription

=item C<tts_language>

Language to be used for text-to-speech

=item C<tts_language_text_normalization>

Whether language-specific text normalization should be applied for text-to-speech True or false.

=item C<tts_provider>

Provider to be used for text-to-speech

=item C<tts_text_normalization>

Text normalization for text-to-speech. The value can be auto, on, or off. Takes precedence over elevenlabsTextNormalization

=item C<turn_detection>

Whether turn detection should be used to decide when the caller has finished speaking. Defaults to false True or false.

=item C<url>

URL of the remote service where the session is connected to

=item C<voice>

Voice to be used for text-to-speech

=item C<welcome_greeting>

The sentence to be played automatically when the session is connected

=item C<welcome_greeting_interruptible>

"Whether and how the input from a caller, such as speaking or DTMF can interrupt the welcome greeting

